From 951b7f110acd472fbea8754c951b8dc2ec5ccaf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds bootstrap <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 06:13:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sound: ARM7 driver and static initializers for the port
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)

The ARM7 sound driver runs on the port sound chip model instead of DS
hardware, and overlay static initializers use a GCC section attribute. The DS
text is unchanged: gcc-10 -E -P of each file without SDK_PORT_3DS (with
-DSDK_ARM7 for sub/, -DSDK_ARM9 for the rest) has 0 diff lines against the
file before this patch. The ARM7 part is rebased from Platinum NitroSDK
0018-0023 against the HGSS driver (sub/lib/src/sound_*.c, a different revision
with unified files); HGSS differences are noted below.

lib/dsprot/include/static_init.h: under SDK_PORT_3DS, NitroStaticInit_ goes in
__attribute__((section(".sinit"), used)) instead of the MWCC section pragmas
(Platinum 0027). The #else keeps the original line order so the Metrowerks
build preprocesses byte-identically. A host object was checked to carry a
.sinit section with the pointer.

sound_main.c (SND_Init): under SDK_PORT_3DS, no ARM7 thread or interval timer;
the subsystems init directly (Command/ExChannel/Seq/Alarm, Enable, output
selector, master volume), as the port audio thread drives the ticks (Platinum
0018). Start/StopIntervalTimer are empty. The dollar-sign statics stay: GCC
accepts them, and the sound data object defines them under the same names, so
no rename is needed. Setup/IsCaptureActive use the port sound array.

sound_command.c (SND_CommandProc): commands are popped with
NitroPort_SoundPopCommand and finishedCommandTag goes up atomically (Platinum
0019); the queue and PXI callback init are skipped, and channel enables call
NitroPort_SoundChannelStart on 0 to 1 only. HGSS differences: the enable bit
lives inline in START_TIMER (there is no SND_StartChannel), so the transition
is checked there; the PCM source keeps all 32 bits (the DS mask is 27).

sound_alarm.c: alarm start/stop go to NitroPort_SoundAlarmStart/Stop with the
(id << 8 | no) message (Platinum 0020); setup only stores. The restart path
stops the old port alarm first, as the DS cancels the old OS alarm.

sound_channel.c and sound_driver.c: register accesses go to
NitroPort_SoundRegisters (Platinum 0018): the R8/R16/R32 macros and the
SOUNDCNT/capture macros are redefined onto the array (indexed from
0x04000400); the direct casts in SetupPsg/Noise, StopChannel and the surround
decay helper are redirected the same way. REG_POWCNT2 is outside the sound
block and stays absolute (sleep paths the port never calls). SND_StopChannel
keeps its read-modify-write shape with a plain word access, since the struct
overlay is addressed from 0x04000000.

sound_ex_channel.c: the SYNC_START enable calls NitroPort_SoundChannelStart
on 0 to 1 (Platinum 0023). Pointers into wave data were already full 32-bit,
as were the bank direct-PCM halves, so no 0021 change was needed beyond the
command mask. sound_bank.c, sound_seq_player.c and sound_shared_work.c need
no changes (no registers, no truncated pointers; shared-work updates already
guard NULL).

lib/NitroSDK/src/snd/SND_work.c: the four ARM9 shared-work getters read under
the port audio spinlock (Platinum 0022), with duplicated bodies (rather than
Platinum null macro) so the Metrowerks build preprocesses byte-identically.

Tests: tests/sdk/arm7_sound/run.sh builds the six ARM7 files plus
sound_shared_work.c, sound_seq_player.c and ARM9 SND_work.c with the survey
flags and runs 42 checks: init order and once-only, the pop-driven command
flow (shared work, starts, PCM pointer, stops, tag), no restarts, alarm
setup/start/restart/stop/id, and the locked getters. Dropping the alarm
restart stop was caught by the suite while writing it. Against the tree
without this patch the suite fails to link.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
